gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config.gcc (i[34567]86-*-*, x86_64-*-*): Add i386-cppbuiltin.o
	to c_target_objs, cxx_target_objs, and fortran_target_objs.
	* config/i386/i386.h (struct cpp_reader): Forward declare.
	(ix86_cpu_cpp_builtins): Declare.
	(TARGET_GENERIC_CPU_CPP_BUILTINS): New hook macro, a
	language-neutral counterpart to TARGET_CPU_CPP_BUILTINS.
	* config/i386/i386-cppbuiltin.h: New file.
	* config/i386/i386-cppbuiltin.cc: New file.  Holds the shared
	pure macro-emission logic formerly in i386-c.cc.
	(ix86_cpp_builtin_define_std): New parameterized helper mirroring
	c-family/c-cppbuiltin.cc's builtin_define_std.
	(ix86_cpu_cpp_builtins_internal): Move from i386-c.cc and take
	cpp_reader as explicit first parameter.
	(ix86_cpu_cpp_builtins): Move from i386-c.cc, take cpp_reader
	and define_user parameters, omit the C++20 STDCPP_FLOAT16 undef
	block (which stays in i386-c.cc).
	* config/i386/i386-c.cc (ix86_target_macros_internal): Delete;
	moved to i386-cppbuiltin.cc as ix86_cpu_cpp_builtins_internal.
	(ix86_target_macros): Shrink to a thin wrapper calling
	ix86_cpu_cpp_builtins, then applying the C++20 STDCPP_FLOAT16
	undef when c_dialect_cxx () && cxx_dialect > cxx20.
	(ix86_pragma_target_parse): Call ix86_cpu_cpp_builtins_internal
	instead of the file-local static helper.
	* config/i386/t-i386: Build i386-cppbuiltin.o.
	* doc/tm.texi.in (TARGET_GENERIC_CPU_CPP_BUILTINS): Document.
	* doc/tm.texi: Regenerate.

gcc/fortran/ChangeLog:

	* cpp.cc (gfc_builtin_define_std): New Fortran-local helper
	mirroring builtin_define_std from c-family/c-cppbuiltin.cc.
	(gfc_builtin_define_with_value): New Fortran-local helper
	mirroring builtin_define_with_value.
	(gfc_darwin_cpp_builtins): New; minimal Darwin platform macros
	that don't depend on c-family functions.
	(cpp_define_builtins): Expose the c-family identifiers needed
	by TARGET_OS_CPP_BUILTINS and TARGET_OBJFMT_CPP_BUILTINS via a
	transient #define block, call those hooks, and invoke the new
	TARGET_GENERIC_CPU_CPP_BUILTINS hook when defined.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gfortran.dg/gomp/declare-variant-10.f90: Remove dead
	__attribute__((target)) block that is exposed by newly
	defined target macros.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-linux.f90: New test.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-x86.f90: New test.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-avx.f90: New test.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-arch.f90: New test.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-fma4.f90: New test.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-cet.f90: New test.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-m32.f90: New test.
	* gfortran.dg/pr42954-soft-float.f90: New test.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
